I really like some of the ideas you've all suggested for mirrors - I'm
glad I mentioned them. Perhaps some of them might find their way into a
future version - who knows?

Telephones are something I've thought about.  If you are really lucky
you'll find a yellow spellbook which allows you to look up those elusive
shopkeepers who would be able to give you their addresses(ie levels),
and which items they have in stock (if you are lucky they'll be
truthful, if not they'll just give you their normal over the top sales
pitch), for instance:-

Upon r(eading) the yellow spellbook:-

Which servies are you interested in (%,=,?,],(,),/,{,#,_)?

You type "?"

The number for Aphonso is 733-6579

If the spellbook's blessed it'll let you have a few more lookups.

Then when you find a 'phone and you a)plly it you get:

What number do you wish to dial (type in 7-digits)?

You type "733-6579"

Hello this is the answer machine for Aphonso's book shop. 
You'll find us on level 14. Today we are speciallising in
scrolls of identify, scrolls labelled VE FORBRYDERNE as well
as out usual stock. We hope to see you soon. Thank you for
calling.


That phone call just cost you $200.


I also included the symbols {, # and _ perhaps these could give you lists
of the nearest levels which contain such things.

I realise that all of these things will start to constrain the actual
dungeon design as we now need to be able to find Aphonso on level 14,
an altar on wherever etc.

There are also services which the telephone could offer which are
not so restrictive:-

Dial 999 (or whatever) and the Keystone Kops turn up - they may attack
you or they may attack whatever's bothering you - I think this will
depend on who is currently in the worst state (hitpoints), alignment and
luck.  This service is free.

Dial an oracle - if you know the number and have the cash you get access
to the regular oracle. There might be a cheaper dial a cookie too.

Dial an object detection, mapping etc - again for cash plus the correct
number you get the equivalent of certain spells, scrolls, potions - this
makes all that gold so easy to spend!  I'm thinking of information based
things only or those which can come as an answer to a call.

And of course if you dial random numbers you may be lucky and get a
goody but you might also get something less pleasant...

I think that there might also be a number you can call which for say
$1000 will give you a wish but after which the telephone goes dead and
all you can hear is an annoying beep (or if having dead 'phones about is
a pain then it vanishes).

The 'phone I've been describing would be an object - perhaps like many
handheld phones it has a rather limited range and to find out more, or
ring say more than +/- 5 levels, you'll need to c(hat) to a phone box -
this might be a type of trap - if you walk into it then its will try to
polymorph you into superman, but if you simply talk to it (and have
enough $s) you can use it as a 'phone with a better range - though I
doubt any phone will work in hell.....  

Perhaps the yellow pages themselves would give you some idea of where
the shops are... or indeed if there are any selling the type of the
thing you were interested in....

What do you think?

Caroline


